## one vendor import without commitids is one trunk commit

Made with CVS 1.12.13: "cvs import" of x, y and z (vendor branch VENDOR,
release tag start), then a trunk commit to x.  The commitid fields were
deleted afterwards, as in repositories written by CVS before 1.12, and the
author was renamed.  There is no CVSROOT, so the conversion runs in RCS mode.

y and z keep "branch 1.1.1;".  cvs-fast-export 2.5 split the import into
two trunk commits at y, and in RCS mode deleted y and z from the vendor
branch commit, so tag start lacked them.  "cvs export -r start" has all
three files.
